 "narrative": "Compared to last report: Trade activity Light. Demand Good to Very Good all markets of hay.  Prices on all classes of hay remained unchanged this period.  Per AAA Fuel Prices website, the diesel fuel current average price across the state is $5.8179/gallon today, down 22 cents from last week, down 80 cents from last month, and up $2.16 from a year ago.  According to the U.S. Drought Monitor's High Plains Summary for November 17, 2026, only targeted changes in drought classification were made over the High Plains states this past week. A small degradation occurred in the Northern Colorado Rockies with a couple small degradations in Eastern Kansas. The most noteworthy degradations were made in Northern and Northeastern Wyoming where well above average temperatures combined with a lack of precipitation led to an expansion of extreme drought as well as an introduction of exceptional drought in northeastern Wyoming. Very poor long-term drought indicators along with ground validation reports suggested the need to introduce this exceptional drought area.  For Drought Classifications, 11.40% of the state falls in Extreme-Exceptional drought (D3-D4) categories, and 88.60% of the state falls into the Abnormally Dry-Severe Drought (D0-D2) categories.  The next available report will be Thursday, December 3, 2026.",
